silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_concrete_anchor_4 silm:hasExample "In 'EnrichmentAnchorDomesticCat', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, DomesticCat is the classification sort: a typed olog node whose only incoming hom-set from Mittens is the singleton {lambda_cls}. For the running fixture the membership statement reads \"Mittens is a DomesticCat\"; the enrichment guarantees that no other arrow Mittens -> DomesticCat is admitted unless explicitly added to the olog. DomesticCat is the species-classification leg, NOT identical to Mittens (no isomorphism) and NOT the taxonomy row TaxRow_TSN183798 — they sit on opposite sides of the apex.." .
